00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:07.390
Hello, my name is Johnathan Roehsner, in this video, I am reviewing Nexventory, the Android

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:12.350
Inventory Application I originally developed in CS360.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:19.190
I'm using this artifact from my CS499 capstone, because it gives me a foundation for demonstrating

00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:25.550
software design and engineering algorithms and data structures, as well as databases

00:00:25.550 --> 00:00:28.950
and one connected project.

00:00:28.950 --> 00:00:36.510
The purpose of this review is to explain how original code works, identify specific weaknesses

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.390
and limitations, and describe the enhancement I plan to make.

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:46.870
I will move through each category in that order, existing functionality, code analysis,

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.710
and plan enhancement.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:53.550
This version already contains more than a visual interface.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:01:02.070
This includes account creation and login code, ASQL Lite database, inventory create,

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:09.750
read, update, and delete operations, as well as low stock SMS logic.

00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:12.550
My enhancements will build on those features.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:18.070
I will be careful to distinguish a feature that already exists from one that is incomplete

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:19.910
or still planned.

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:26.270
For example, the app displays a search field, but that does not mean inventory searching

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:32.830
